==English==

===Etymology===
First attested about 1860, in the US, as a fanciful alteration of {{m|en|lick}} and the verb {{m|en|split}}. {{m|en|lick}} appears to have something to do with animals made to go faster by means of a "lick" of a whip, although it may have also originated due to a preference for rapid licking (the "quick lick").

